# Portable skill docs - tracker stays in issues

Applies to **every tracked `.md` file** in this repo - skills, reference, bootstrap, release notes, and other operational docs. The only carve-out is **gitignored** markdown.

Much of this repo ships to **other repos** via skill install. Keep the **tracker layer** (GitHub issues, map bodies, bundle/task comments) separate from **committed markdown** here.

## In tracked markdown

Use **generic placeholders** - never anchors that bind to this repo or a specific map instance.

| Write | Not |
| --- | --- |
| `{MAP-SLUG}-GM-001` with a fictional slug (`CMD-PAL`, `SEARCH-PANEL`) | `WF-ECO-GM-028`, `GM-024`, or any slug from a live map in this repo |
| `#N`, `org/repo`, `{FeatureName}:Map` | `https://github.com/KroniK907/skills/issues/N` or `#29` pointing at this repo |
| "the map issue", "the bundle issue", "Parent: …" as prose | Markdown links to issues in `KroniK907/skills` |

**Format examples** teach shape; **instance examples** pin a reader to one map. Prefer fictional slugs and `#N` over real decision-log rows or issue numbers from Wayfinder-Ecosystem or sibling maps.

## Where issue and GM references belong

Put concrete links and decision-log rows in the **tracker**, not in committed markdown here:

- Map, bundle, task, and decision-log **issue bodies**
- **Comments** on those issues (resolution, reconcile, research findings)

When a skill needs a worked example, describe the pattern in prose or use placeholders - point humans to the live map issue for real IDs.

## Author checklist

Before committing skill or reference markdown:

- [ ] No live issue URLs from this repo (`KroniK907/skills/issues/N`)
- [ ] GM examples use fictional slugs (`CMD-PAL-GM-001`), not rows from a live map
- [ ] Format examples use `#N` and `{FeatureName}:Map`, not pinned instance IDs

Domain skills with real worked examples (e.g. ccr-summary) may keep factual contact data when the example is the point.
